WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:02.090
- Okay, you know what?

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.220
Actually, I wanted to
give a special shout out

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.239
to my kids' grandparents.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.607
Arie and Coco Kopelman, that's right.

00:00:09.607 --> 00:00:12.060
(audience cheering)

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.300
I love them so much and it
was Arie's birthday this week

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.170
so we've been doing a lot
of celebrating of Poppy

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.600
and that's Grammy.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.730
And I have to tell you they
told me that they've been

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.740
watching the show and they
are supremely honest with me.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.190
Like when Arie doesn't get something

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.330
he just flat out says it.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.100
And which is this great 'cause
I always know where I stand

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.430
with them and they're
worldly and I really trust

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.820
their opinion and tastes and honestly,

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.310
I wanna make them proud and
they're loving the show.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.453
So hi guys, I love you.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.030
Now, do we have any
grandparents in our VFFs today?

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.600
Joyce?

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.260
- Hi, how are you Drew?

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.123
- Hi Joyce?

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.730
- How are you?

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.910
- Arie always says
there's nothing overrated

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.560
about being a grandparent.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.550
That's one of his famous quotes.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.930
He's the kind of guy too
who everywhere he goes

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.543
he walks around and he
goes, isn't this the best?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.920
It's the greatest thing.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.230
So I call them Grammy and Poppy.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.423
Do you have a grandparent nickname?

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:16.110
- I do, my grandchildren
Alice, Andrew and Branson,

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.000
they call me Mimi.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.500
I asked to be called Gramssy
but they call Mimi so,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.303
one happy Mimi am I.

00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:24.136
(audience laughs)

00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:26.540
- Well, there were definitely
pre-existing family members

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.950
who chose Grammy and Poppy so,

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.530
I was just lucky to get on the train

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.640
and I'm so glad to meet you
Joyce and thank you for sharing.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.037
- Thank you, here say to
my little Mimi something.

00:01:35.037 --> 00:01:36.323
- Oh,

00:01:37.345 --> 00:01:38.400
(Joyce laughing)

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.742
well congratulations on being
an excellent grandparent.

00:01:41.742 --> 00:01:43.110
- Thank you and
congratulations on your show.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:43.943
- Thank you, Joyce.

00:01:43.943 --> 00:01:46.380
All right, we've got a big show today

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.840
helping me close out our
second show of the week

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.600
is a wonderful, sweet, kind
and very funny friend of mine.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.460
We were also married once,
his name is Tom Green.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.440
And you know, it's a moment

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.010
I'm excited to share it with you.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.580
All right and we wanna shine a light

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.990
on all the wild flowers out there.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.080
All of the girls and
women who are breaking

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.430
down walls and making
their own paths to success.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.620
And today we meet Sky Brown
who is a young skateboarder

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.920
and she is so brave.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.960
And man, she's about to tell
us something that trusts me

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.010
you just don't want to miss
it, it blew my hair back.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.780
So let's first get into some
information about the world

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.380
we live in, it's time
for some Drew's News.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.533
(audience cheering)

00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:33.873
(tire squeals)
(cat meows)

00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:37.041
(dramatic music)

00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:38.374
Sir, Ma'am, guy.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.693
Ma'am, I asked you a question.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.073
It's Drew's News.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:50.077
All right, let's see what made the papers.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.000
First, okay this is actually
sort of a very important

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.530
periodical to me growing up.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.170
TV Guide has a section
called Cheers and Jeers.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.970
And I even talked to a
journalist recently and was like,

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.810
Cheers and Jeers, it's
like, it's still out there

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.140
and it's in the latest issue of TV Guide.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.250
And this week, guess what guys?

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.650
I'm so excited to share
this with everyone here.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.988
Our show made the Cheers section.

00:03:17.988 --> 00:03:19.244
(audience cheering)

00:03:19.244 --> 00:03:20.470
Phew.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.323
Oh my gosh, I'm not kidding.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.133
Phew.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.120
Damian Holbrook said that we
had a divinely inspired launch.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.350
I mean, this is such a big deal for me.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.140
When I was a kid I
would savor my TV Guides

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.300
and I always looked to
the Cheers and Jeers

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.720
for what was like good
or couldn't be missed.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.640
And it's a tradition
that's still going on.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.140
I'm not kidding, I check
in regularly about it.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.890
So cheers right back at
you Damian and TV Guide.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.911
Thank you for the props,
that means a lot to us.

00:03:51.911 --> 00:03:53.340
(audience cheering)

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.167
So I'm so excited for
this news I just saw.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:59.750
"Father of the Bride"'s gang
is getting back together.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.580
Today Netflix is dropping
"Father of the Bride"

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.160
We'll call it part three.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.210
Steve Martin, Diane Keaton,
Kimberly Williams-Paisley

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.610
Martin Short, Kieran
Culkin and Nancy Meyers,

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.590
the writer, director
herself they're all back

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.700
and the reunion is benefiting
World Central Kitchen

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.752
who happens to be with friend
of the show, Jose Andres.

00:04:19.752 --> 00:04:20.600
(audience cheering)

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.650
That's right.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.880
Changing the world he is.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.840
And a fun fact, I have the
DVD in our really old ancient

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.350
minivan and I play the movie
for the kids all the time.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.750
And to this day, I get
very verklempt every time

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.150
Steve Martin is doing his
voiceovers 'cause obviously

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.970
I can't be watching while I'm
driving but I hear him talking

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.050
about the house they grew
up in and how it's like cool

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.260
in the summer and warm in the
winters and anytime you hear

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.550
a father talking about their
daughter this way I mean,

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.750
I'm just telling you oh, it's so good.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.100
So I'm gonna be checking
that out, maybe you can too.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.750
Okay, I don't mean to stress you out

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.073
but we're almost a month
away from Halloween.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.620
Have you thought of a costume?

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.020
Have you thought of one
for your guinea pig?

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.610
Well, don't freak out yet
because Popsugar has posted

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.820
a guide to PetSmart's fun
and affordable costumes

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.050
for all your furball friends.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.350
Oh, you don't have a guinea pig?

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.580
Oh, you don't care?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.200
Well, we're gonna look at
all these photos anyway.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.190
All right, first up for a traditionalist.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.520
Here's a lovely pumpkin boy.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:30.220
Oh, hi pumpkin boy,
there you are, oh yeah.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.733
And then there's unicorn
princess, look at her.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:41.520
And there's also a bumblebee
and a lobster and a baby dino.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.960
Look at this cuties.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.270
Oh, and here's one more costume

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.030
I wanted to just show you guys.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.373
Oh, there you are, hi.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.580
I'm telling you we're running
wild kingdom at my house.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:59.140
Like my kids are always you know,

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.340
especially Olive's nickname
is literally Ace Ventura.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.920
We're actually gonna do a
segment called Dr. Drew Little

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.280
because let's face it,
when your kids get pets,

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.610
you get pets.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.330
All right so this one, I got the hot dog,

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.090
by the way this is Daisy, she's a boy.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.600
